 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
+## Thresholds (CI Gating)
+- `generateReport` accepts an optional `thresholds` object mapping metric IDs to minimum scores (0–1).
+- If supplied, the report includes a `passed` boolean and a `thresholds` array with per-metric pass/fail status.
+- Metrics with no score (due to missing references, etc.) fail their thresholds instead of crashing.
+- Markdown reports gain a "Thresholds" section showing `PASS` or `FAIL` for each threshold.
+- CLI `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option can be used multiple times. Exit code: 0 if all pass, 1 if any fail, 2 for usage errors.
+- Without thresholds, reports and exit codes remain unchanged.
+
 ## Follow-up Tasks
 1. Integrate real toxicity/bias models once provider abstraction is implemented (Phase 0 → Providers milestone).
 2. Extend datasets loader to support configurable schema mapping.
